WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:10.990
Please don't expect too much from it.
This story is a simple illustration of the three
Minami sisters and the ordinary life they lead.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.620
Hey, Kana, are you ready?

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.180
That should do it.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.690
Thanks, Haruka.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:21.610
Well?

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:24.620
What do you think of your beautiful
older sister in a long-sleeved kimono?

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:28.230
That's not how you pronounce
"annoying older sister."

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:31.260
Haruka-neesama, you look great in yours.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.160
Thank you.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.880
You look cute too.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.630
Take this!

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:42.560
Noooo!

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.440
What're you doing?

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.590
My hand slipped because you were acting
.cheeky toward your beautiful older sister.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:50.940
Why, you!

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.370
Wait! Stop running!

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.960
Gotta catch me first!

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.620
I said, stop!

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:58.640
Kana!

00:00:58.640 --> 00:00:59.540
Now, now. No fighting on New Year's.
Kana!

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.450
Get back here!
Now, now. No fighting on New Year's.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:01.870
Catch me if you can!
Now, now. No fighting on New Year's.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.830
Catch me if you can!

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.250
You!

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.170
Noooo!

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:12.810
U-Um...

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.590
Haruka-neesama...

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:16.800
This was an... um...

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.890
Don't worry, I know.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.810
It's not your fault, Chiaki.

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:26.290
Chiaki! Let's turn Kana around!

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:27.310
Roger!

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.330
Take this!

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:31.570
Noooo!

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:34.180
Happy New Year!

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:35.540
Joy, warmth, and cheer!

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:37.200
Thanks for having us.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.610
Sob, sob.

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.450
Now I can't be a bride.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:41.740
Oh, welcome...

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.320
What're you doing?

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.140
It was like an old samurai movie.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:47.250
It's New Year's. What the heck are you doing?

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:50.700
We're putting on our kimonos. Could you wait a minute?

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.940
All right! Let's enjoy the new year!

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:02.560
Yeah!

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:36.980
Start Planning Your Year from New Year's Day

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.970
New
Year's
Gift

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.720
Happy New Year!

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:11.520
I'm Sensei!

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.380
And I'm Ninomiya-kun!

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:16.060
Happy New Year!

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:18.690
We're going all out this year too!

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:21.650
All right, Sensei. Let's whip
out the party tricks!

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:27.660
I'll be using this umbrella to
.turn Ninomiya-kun around.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.910
And I'll be turned by the umbrella.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.320
All right, let's do it!

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:32.080
All right!

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.120
There! Ready, go!

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:33.790
Ninomiya-kun!

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:34.620
Sensei!

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:35.500
Ninomiya-kun!

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.000
Sensei!

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.670
Ninomiya-kun! Ninomiya-kun!
Uchida, how many mochi do you want?

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:38.790
Noooo!

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:39.920
Two.
Noooo!

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:40.210
Two.

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:48.100
We went to the shrine.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.850
We got New Year's money.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:52.020
We flew kites and spun tops.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.840
And then you came to our
.place like you do every day.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:56.520
Huh?

00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:00.190
You even had two mochi in your soup.

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:02.360
Everything's supposed to come in pairs.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.280
It's the same reason you get two <i>kan</i> of sushi on a plate.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.660
This isn't sushi boat!

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:10.120
Wow. You knew a piece of
sushi was called a <i>kan</i>?

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:15.620
You're eating a lot of mochi
.at someone else's place.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.050
You're drinking up the red bean soup without leaving a drop.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.340
And now you're going to sleep.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.600
We took this picture in the summer.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.080
Oh, when we went to the beach.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.810
That was fun.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.230
Yes it was, Haruka-neesama.

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:43.230
And this was your belly in the summer.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:47.150
I wonder what kind of disaster it is now.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:51.160
I-It's not <i>that</i> bad...

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:55.160
All right! We're going to an
indoor pool tomorrow!

00:05:55.160 --> 00:06:00.710
Provided you haven't been living a slothful,
gluttonous New Year's, you should have no objections!

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:08.010
But why the pool all of a sudden?

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:10.850
Kana just decided she wanted to go to one.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:13.560
Kana-chan's always deciding things on a whim.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:18.310
All right. Why don't we get some
swim practice in for the summer?

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:20.020
Yoshino, help me out.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.020
Okay.

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:22.770
Hey, you two!

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:26.480
Stop, Kana-chan! Let me go!

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:27.780
Well? How's her belly?

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.910
It's not my fault!

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.780
It's the mochi's fault for being so delicious!

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:35.300
Well? Well? How is it?

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:35.790
Well?

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:39.120
Well, yeah...

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.040
No real difference.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.170
Now I can't be a bride.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:45.050
Shoot.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:49.300
We came all the way to the pool,
but now we're out of things to do.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:52.470
We really just came here for that?

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:58.060
I wanted to put Uchida through intensive training
...to get rid of that embarrassing stomach flab, too...

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:00.640
Training...

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:02.770
Hey, Uchida.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.480
What do you call that huge,
flabby stomach of yours?

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:07.900
Huh? Didn't you just say there wasn't much of a difference?

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:11.200
You need to cut down on
...that flab immediately...

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:15.700
with a warm-water diet
.training course from Hell!

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.660
What's up, Chiaki?

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:20.120
You look like you're really set on this.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:26.880
Thinking back, I just realized that I've trained to swim before, but I've never trained someone to swim before.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.880
I want to train someone!

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:29.970
I see.

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:33.220
From now on, call me the
Demon Instructor from Hell!

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:35.720
I can call you that, but...

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:38.180
Do you remember, Uchida?

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:40.230
Last year, when we went to
..the pool for gym class...

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:44.310
Don't let go!

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:45.730
Promise me!

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:47.110
Okay, okay.

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:56.660
Thanks to your clumsy feet, I...

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.040
I...

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:59.160
I'm sorry.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:00.960
That's why you need training!

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:03.120
It's revenge!

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.210
You're just calling your revenge "training"!

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:08.250
Yoshino, help me!

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:14.510
Hey, Demon Instructor, can we do the training after lunch?

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:15.510
What?!

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:19.350
Oh, right. I heard the food
.here was pretty good.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:20.520
Haruka said so.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.560
The ice cream's good too.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.020
Ice cream in the winter,
huh? That's living big!

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:32.030
All right, let's get that lunch!

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:34.070
Yeah!

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:39.240
Thanks for the meal!

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:41.580
That was so good!

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.750
Haruka-chan really knows her stuff.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:44.580
Yeah.

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:46.460
Maybe we can invite Keiko,
Riko, and Miyuki next time.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:48.630
Why didn't you invite them today?

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:50.840
They're all on trips or seeing family.

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:53.220
That sounds great.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:55.430
I wish I could go on a trip.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:56.360
Then how about...

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.690
another two-day, one-night trip to the Minami household?

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:00.220
M-Maybe some other time.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:01.600
Speaking of which...

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:08.270
Feels like you're the one who needs the most training, Chiaki.

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:09.610
Who's Chiaki?

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.070
Call me the Demon Instructor.

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:14.320
Now then, we've had a fulfilling meal.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.780
The Demon Instructor
.will be taking a nap.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:19.280
The Demon Instructor sure is lazy.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:21.830
<b>Locker Room</b>

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:28.130
Huh?

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:33.210
It was really big!

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:34.840
At least <i>this</i> big!

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.590
I think the one I saw was a bit smaller.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:40.050
But it was really pretty!

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:43.520
Those two went on trips
.overseas during winter break.

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:48.020
Sounds like they saw some famous buildings.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.400
Ain't that nice.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.520
I got a hankerin' to go overseas too.

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:53.440
Huh?

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:56.820
Did you go somewhere, Riko?

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.300
Jus' went to old grammy's.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:03.120
And your grandma's place is pretty far away?

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:07.040
Yeah, you could say that.
Kyoto ain't close, at least.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.920
I see. Kyoto.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:12.590
Hey, Kana-chan! It was really big!

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:13.880
Okay, sure.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:16.050
So, what was the building called?

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.100
Huh?

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:19.050
I forget.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:21.260
How'd you jus' forget?

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.720
Where'd you go anyway, Miyuki-chan?

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:26.850
I forget.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:29.140
How'd you forget that?

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:31.400
What about you, Keiko?
Where'd you go?

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:34.940
Huh?

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:36.240
Earth to Keiko!

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:39.610
What? Sorry, I was spacing out.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:41.140
Thinking about something?

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:45.860
It's the third term, so we're going to have the school marathon, right?

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:47.660
I get so depressed just thinking about it.

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:48.710
Huh?

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:51.420
How long was the school marathon again?

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.790
I think it was six miles.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:57.090
Oh, that's all? I thought
.it was twenty-six miles.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:59.180
Why're y'all countin' in miles now?

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:01.890
You just need to start training right away.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.180
I mean, we've got another
.school check-up in the spring.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:06.100
You can think of it as like a diet.

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.810
Y-Yeah, you're right.

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:10.520
I put on four pounds over the break.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.190
If we don't get it together,
it'll be a hundred pounds.

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:14.110
Why're y'all countin' in pounds?!

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:16.220
It don't make no sense!

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:18.860
Why can't y'all be usin'
kilometers and kilograms?

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:21.450
Yeah, you're right.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:24.070
We have to snap out of the
.overseas thing at some point.

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:26.630
Snap out of the overseas thing?

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:28.410
Sorry, Riko-chan.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:29.750
Sorry.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:32.880
Naw, it's alright.
As long as y'all understand.

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:34.880
Hey, overseas girls.

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:39.510
Riko isn't snapping out of her Kyoto thing.

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:41.320
You think she realizes?

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:41.980
Huh?

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:43.010
What do you mean?

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:44.860
Riko-chan's talking like she usually does.

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:45.640
No way!

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:50.720
But you know, thinkin' about the marathon and
.school check-up leaves me feelin' mighty blue.

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:52.020
Ain't that the truth.

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:53.060
It's contagious?!

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:56.070
This leaves me no choice. It's time for...

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.780
What's up, Minami?

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:02.950
Help me out, Fujioka.
They've all gone to Kyoto.

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:04.280
Kyoto?

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:06.780
How many kilometers was a marathon 'gain?

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.040
I'm thinkin' it might be ten.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:12.870
Really? I was thinkin' it was 42.15 kilometers.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:15.040
Ain't that a full marathon?!

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.170
You two're makin' like twins today.

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:20.420
Sure, but how much weight'll
a marathon lose you?

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:23.180
Ain't gonna make a diff'rence if you don't keep at 'er every day, I say.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:27.300
It'd sure be nice if you lost two kilos every ten kilos you ran.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.280
Ain't that the truth.

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:30.810
Talking about the marathon?

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:32.520
Oh, Fujioka-kun?

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:33.770
Th-That's right.

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:34.980
It's almost that time of year again.

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:37.230
Better get ready for it good.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.840
Fujioka-kun's smile!

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:43.070
Oh, Fujioka-kun, did you get a bit of a tan?

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:44.740
Did you go somewhere over the break?

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:46.420
Oh, does it show?

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:49.790
I went snowboarding over
.break and got a snow tan.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:50.700
Really?

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:51.790
That sounds nice.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.500
It looks like a beard!

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:54.710
How are you? Any good?

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:56.220
No, not really...

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:57.380
Huh?

00:12:57.730 --> 00:13:01.130
Oh, good! You're all back from Kyoto!

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:03.590
Whatcha mean, back?

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:04.820
Y'all're back!

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:07.220
You jus' went back to it now!

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:08.760
You're talking weird, Kana.

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:10.540
I've had enough o' this!

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:26.450
I'm telling you, we gotta have a hot pot.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:27.490
Let's have one.

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:29.450
A hot pot, huh...

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:32.790
It's cold out, but just going straight for the hot pot is too boring.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.120
Why don't we think of something else?

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:35.660
Sure, let's do a hot pot.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:36.750
It's simple enough.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:39.250
Yeah, we gotta have hot pot, Haruka-neesama!

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:41.500
Hot pot's the best on chilly days like these!

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:42.380
Hey.

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:47.510
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:52.470
We have visitors.

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:55.040
Hey, Chiaki! Haruka-chan!

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:57.020
Let's go play outside!

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:58.520
The snow's amazing.

00:13:58.520 --> 00:13:59.940
Let's have a snowball fight!

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:04.280
Huh?

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:06.160
There's tons of snow outside.
Don't you know?

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:07.280
No, we do.

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:10.620
That's why we're all warm and toasty under the kotatsu.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.300
Come on, let's get out of the kotatsu!

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:16.540
Quit it!

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:19.080
I may not look it,
but I get cold easily!

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:24.510
I may look it, but I need to prepare myself before I can leave a kotatsu!

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:26.090
It's fine, it's fine.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.240
Haruka-chan, what're you writing?

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:31.090
Just one second.

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:32.350
Here, Kana.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:34.350
Huh? What's this?

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:37.350
Since you're going out, could
you pick those up for me?

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:42.610
Guess it's already decided
.that <i>she's</i> not coming.

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:45.940
I may not look it, but I'm quite busy.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:46.780
You sure are.

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:50.860
Busy getting warm in the kotatsu and warming up the kotatsu.

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:54.200
All right, let's go, Chiaki.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.540
What?

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:58.300
I'm counting on you too, Chiaki.

00:14:58.300 --> 00:14:59.920
Yes, Haruka-neesama!

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.540
All right, we'll be back.

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:07.260
Wow, it sure has piled up.

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:08.170
You're right.

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:12.280
Touma, why are you making a snowball?

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:15.720
We've got snow, so we need
.to have a snowball fight.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:17.560
You really are a hooligan.

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:19.430
Why don't we <i>all</i> decide
what we want to play?

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:22.150
But I already made one...

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:24.770
Oh, it may not look it,
but this is a rice ball.

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:25.690
Would you like to eat it?

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:27.150
No, thank you.

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:28.400
Throw it away.

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:38.830
Fine.

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:42.040
You want a snowball fight? Is that it?

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:44.330
Fine by me. Snowball fight it is.

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:46.750
I'll take you all down at once!

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:47.840
Come at me!

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:50.300
I may not look it, but I've got a good arm!

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:52.760
Not good enough!

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:55.220
I may not look it, but I watch a lot of baseball!

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:58.180
That's a softball pitch...

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.680
I may not look it, but I like soccer more!

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:01.690
Ow!

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.490
You've got a lot of nerve!

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:11.820
Now it's my—

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:13.320
Here we go, Kana-chan!

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:14.820
Here's a forkball!

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:18.080
Elementary vs junior high!

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:19.240
W-Wait.

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:20.830
I'm the only one in junior high...

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:22.370
Here it comes!

00:16:23.510 --> 00:16:25.380
Quit it!

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:31.220
Why did I have to end up like this?!

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:33.740
Because it was elementary vs junior high.

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:34.720
That's no fair!

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:36.970
And you know,

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:39.720
I may not look it, but I haven't lost yet!

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.230
Just admit defeat.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:43.730
Kana!

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:46.690
Haruka! You came for
the snowball fight too?

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.060
You forgot your wallet.

00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:50.230
Oh.

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:53.240
And here's some more things to buy.

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:57.570
Since you came all the way out here, why don't you come too?

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:00.370
I may not look it, but I'm actually very busy.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.960
All right, I'm counting on you.

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:04.870
She's going back to the kotatsu...

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:09.090
Sisters out.

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:22.640
That really hurt!

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:40.660
Bean-Throwing Festival?

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:42.910
What's this Bean-Throwing Festival?

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:46.290
Have you never done it before, Mako-chan?

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:48.920
The Bean-Throwing Festival is, simply put,

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:55.420
when we throw beans around the house to ward demons off and call luck in.

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:57.220
I'm surprised, Kana.

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:58.680
You actually know about it.

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:00.430
I see.

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:04.470
First Halloween, and now this? We're getting a ton of fancy holidays these days.

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:06.690
The bean-throwing festival has been around since the Ashikaga Shogunate.

00:18:07.170 --> 00:18:09.940
All right, I'll play the role of the demon!

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:15.280
Here. You shout "Demons out!" while throwing these beans at the demon.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:16.190
Got it!

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:19.240
Demons out!

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.780
Demons out!

00:18:23.190 --> 00:18:24.540
Not good enough!

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:28.000
You'll need a billion beans to beat me!

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:30.200
That's too much!

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:33.340
No average home would
have that many beans!

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:36.080
Demons out!

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:40.840
It doesn't have to be beans?

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:41.680
Nope.

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:42.760
Here.

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:46.020
Hey, no bears allowed!

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:48.350
Demons out!

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:50.270
Luck in!

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:52.190
Not good enough!

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:54.020
Bring those billion beans!

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:57.650
We sure threw them.

00:18:57.650 --> 00:18:59.060
We sure did.

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:01.030
You sure threw them.

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:02.740
I'm home.

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:07.950
I told you not to throw too many beans.

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:09.540
I'm sorry!

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:12.080
Clean it up and I'll prepare a snack for us.

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:13.540
Yes!

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:24.810
A demon is picking up beans.

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:29.890
A Minami family special: lucky rollcake.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.100
Here, Mako-chan.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:32.150
Thanks!

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:34.400
Let's eat!

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:39.400
The Bean-Throwing Festival isn't half bad.

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:42.410
One isn't enough! We demand more!

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:43.680
Here, Kana.

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:44.910
Yay!

00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:49.380
Could it be that the demon is greedy?

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:52.560
It's a demon. Of course they're greedy.

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:54.670
Kana, let me see that mask.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:55.920
Here.

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:57.920
One more slice please!

00:19:57.920 --> 00:19:59.550
Here, Mako-chan.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:00.670
Yay!

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.880
Would you like another one too, Chiaki?

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:04.390
Sure.

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:07.040
Wait, she's not a demon, but she still got one.

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:11.310
Now then, maybe I should
.make a start on dinner.

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:17.570
Hey, demon,

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:19.440
how long are you going to stay here?

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:20.190
Huh?

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:21.320
Demons out, remember?

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:25.320
A-Are you going to kick me out?

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:29.200
Well, if you're a useful demon, maybe we can keep you.

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:31.160
I can be useful!

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:31.910
All right.

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:33.720
Demon, get me more coffee.

00:20:33.720 --> 00:20:34.680
Right away.

00:20:35.390 --> 00:20:36.330
Here.

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:39.300
Hey, demon.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:40.090
Rub my shoulders.

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:42.720
You're working the demon too hard.

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:44.130
Hey, demon.

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:46.470
I'm done with my coffee,
so grab me a juice, will ya?

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:47.600
You're more of a demon than me!

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:49.260
I can't take it anymore!

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:51.350
You're too moody! I'm out of here!

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:53.020
Mako-chan.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:55.350
Once a demon goes soft,
their life is over.

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.110
Chiaki...

00:20:57.470 --> 00:21:00.860
Allow me to show you
.how to be a real demon.

00:21:01.270 --> 00:21:02.030
Okay.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:04.020
Hey, demon.

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:05.610
Got my juice yet?

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:08.120
Get it yourself, moron.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:09.530
All right, then rub my shoulders.

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:11.620
Do it yourself, moron.

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:13.320
All right, then clean the bath.

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:15.500
It's your turn to do it, moron.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:17.830
That's not a demon at all.

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:19.660
It's just the usual Chiaki.

00:21:19.660 --> 00:21:23.380
Now, I'll go help Haruka-neesama.

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:27.140
That's just the usual Chiaki!

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:32.890
Oh, right.

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:34.890
Chiaki, could you peel these for me?

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:36.690
Yes.

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.020
H-Haruka-neesama!

00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:42.190
Hm?

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:46.780
No carrots today!

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:50.030
Too bad.

00:23:20.950 --> 00:23:24.670
Next episode: "What's Said Here, Stays Here."

00:23:24.670 --> 00:23:26.840
And what we're saying is...

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:29.040
No, I can't tell you yet!

00:23:29.040 --> 00:23:31.220
I bet it's not that big a deal.

00:23:31.220 --> 00:23:33.300
Now, now, Chiaki.
